    dct:description "Global paleoclimate archives directly and independently measure temperature and ice history. They provide sufficient temporal and spatial coverage to resolve the broad simultaneous-cooling claim." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Align independently dated temperature and ice-volume proxies from both hemispheres and across longitudes during the last glacial cycle. Test whether their credible intervals show an overlapping globally cooler interval versus asynchronous regional glaciations." ;
